                <pb facs="0956" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.796/5 supp.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-10T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your telegram No. 5, February 17, 1 p.m., and Department’s telegram No. 5,
                    March 3, 6 p.m., in reply.</p>
                <p>Endeavor in an informal and discreet manner to ascertain the attitude of the
                    Government of Venezuela toward the establishment by American interests of
                    commercial air lines in Venezuela, or air lines connecting Venezuela with
                    neighboring nations and the United States. Without further definite
                    instructions, do not make any statement which could possibly be interpreted as
                    favoring any specific interest or any particular project.</p>
                <p>This information is desired by the Department simply for its guidance when
                    advising American interests which may inquire as to the probable attitude of the
                    Government of Venezuela toward the possible extension of air lines to Venezuela
                    or the establishment of air lines within that country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
